MCP::Hub::Aggregate::_wrap_tool (lib/MCP/Hub/Aggregate.pm:35) builds the prefixed Facade::Tool from name/description/input_schema/output_schema/annotations only — the tool's `extra` (title, icons, _meta) is not carried over, and Aggregate is a plain MCP::Server that does not re-merge it. Found during k29 research: a tool with title and _meta shows both on its own endpoint, neither on /all. Breaks the hazard 'the façade must not drop extra'; present since v1, no test covers it. Needs a regression test (mcp-hub-test-writer) and the fix (mcp-hub-worker).

Regression test added: t/aggregate.t (3 subtests; controls on the own endpoint pass, every /all assertion for tool and prompt title/icons/_meta fails on HEAD). Fix: Aggregate::_wrap_tool/_wrap_prompt must carry extra, and the aggregate needs a Facade::Server-style merging list render (it is a plain MCP::Server). Not committed, not handed off.

Regression test added: t/aggregate.t (3 subtests; the controls on the own endpoint pass, all /all assertions for tool and prompt title/icons/_meta fail on HEAD). Fix goes in Aggregate::_wrap_tool/_wrap_prompt plus an extra-merging list render on the aggregate (see Facade::Server). Not committed, not handed off.

2026-11-06 01:34 Cause, wider than the card says: for an in-process class (the test's ExtraEcho, Upstream::Perl) the upstream server is the class itself with plain MCP::Tool objects -- there is no Facade::Tool->extra to copy; the extras exist only in what that server renders in its own tools/list / prompts/list. So the fix takes them from the upstream's own render at rebuild time (works for façades and in-process alike), stores them on the wrapped Facade::Tool / the aggregate's extra->{prompts}, and makes Aggregate a Facade::Server subclass so its list render re-merges them (after the tools-event filter).

